---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy">
  <h2>Privacy posture</h2>
  <p>
    Trace Commons is privacy-preserving by design. Three properties of this site
    you can rely on:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Opt-in attribution.</strong> A contributor's handle only appears on
      this site if they have explicitly opted in via the <code>public_attribution</code>
      consent scope. The default is private. Their pseudonymous identifier is never
      published.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Aggregate-only analytics.</strong> Corpus dashboards apply min-cell
      thresholds and Laplace noise before publication. No per-trace details, no
      cross-tenant joins beyond the configured budget.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Withdrawal is immediate.</strong> Withdrawing public attribution
      removes a contributor's handle from the leaderboard and their profile page
      at the next snapshot (≤15 minutes). Database rows persist as soft-deletes
      so the audit chain stays intact, but no public surface displays them.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What is shown</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Self-declared handle.</li>
    <li>Self-declared bio (optional, ≤280 bytes).</li>
    <li>The contributor's <em>aggregate</em> counts: accepted submissions, credit, rolling windows.</li>
    <li>The date the contributor first opted in.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is not shown</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Raw envelope content. Ever.</li>
    <li>Per-trace tool sequences linked to a handle.</li>
    <li>Anything about contributors who have not opted in.</li>
    <li>Tenant identifiers or operator-secret material.</li>
    <li>Real-name identity. Handles are self-declared.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Withdrawing</h2>
  <p>
    The <a href="/profile">profile page</a> (shipping in slice 3) exposes a
    "withdraw public attribution" action that takes effect at the next snapshot.
    Until that ships, ask the pilot operator to revoke your profile manually.
  </p>
</Base>
